# EpiGraph Explorer — append inside the public site block of the VM Caddyfile,
# next to the existing epigraph-api stanzas (same pattern as services/nli).
# Assumes the explorer listens on 127.0.0.1:8096 on the same host: either the
# systemd unit (epigraph-explorer.service.example) or a --network host
# container. The binary binds loopback only, so Caddy is the public edge.
#
# PREFIX STRIPPING. `handle_path` strips the matched `/explorer` prefix before
# proxying, so the explorer receives `/claim/<id>`, not
# `/explorer/claim/<id>`. It cannot recover the prefix from the request, so
# EPIGRAPH_EXPLORER_PUBLIC_BASE_URL must carry it, e.g.
#   EPIGRAPH_EXPLORER_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://explorer.example.com/explorer
# Every link, redirect, og:url, the cookie Path and the OAuth redirect_uri
# (`.../explorer/auth/callback`, which must match the oauth_clients row
# byte for byte) are generated from it. The explorer also answers on the
# unstripped paths, so `handle /explorer* { ... }` works too; pick one.
#
# /oauth/* MUST STAY BROWSER-REACHABLE. Sign-in is the API's own OAuth
# authorization server, and the browser navigates to it directly:
#   GET  /oauth/authorize            (explorer -> API, with PKCE)
#   GET  /oauth/callback             (Google -> API)
#   POST /oauth/authorize/consent    (the consent form's root-relative action)
# These live at the root of the API's EPIGRAPH_PUBLIC_BASE_URL and are
# already exposed for the claude.ai connector. Do not move them behind this
# prefix, and do not let a broader matcher here shadow them. Point
# EPIGRAPH_OAUTH_BASE_URL at that browser-facing API origin. Only /api/v1 can
# stay hidden behind the explorer (it reaches the API on loopback via
# EPIGRAPH_API_URL). The explorer's own sign-in routes are /explorer/auth/*,
# which are distinct from the API's /oauth/*.
#
# HEADERS. The explorer sets its own Content-Security-Policy, including
# `frame-ancestors` (the Notion embed depends on it), X-Content-Type-Options
# and Referrer-Policy. Do not add X-Frame-Options or a second CSP for this
# path in Caddy: a site-wide `X-Frame-Options: DENY` breaks the embed. Do not
# strip the Origin request header (Caddy forwards it by default): POST
# /auth/logout compares it with the public origin.

handle_path /explorer* {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8096
}
